Z||000000||FIERO1985||12-06-2000||06:11 PM||||How do you remove an antenna on an 85 gt I am replacing it<P>thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||fropuff||12-06-2000||06:28 PM||||If you're talking about the mast part of it, it just screws off.  Just use an adjustabe wrench and turn to the left.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||FIERO1985||12-06-2000||06:35 PM||||really I am having problems getting the mast off, it just screws undone from the base.?||||reg||1
Z||000003||sqoach||12-06-2000||06:44 PM||||i was having trouble getting mine off too. i tried some pliers but they didn't stay tight and i didn't have much leverage. i ended up using a pair of visegrips to get mine off. just tighten down on that sucker and make sure you turn it counter clockwise. try some wd-40 also. you'll get it.<P>------------------<BR>sQoaCh<BR>fiero7@hotmail.com<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mysig_2.JPG">  <p>[This message has been edited by sqoach (edited 12-06-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||FIERO1985||12-06-2000||06:56 PM||||thanks<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Old Lar||12-06-2000||08:29 PM||||You should be able to remove it with a 10mm box wrench.  If it doesn't loosen and you crank on it, you break the mast stud.  Then you get to loosen the fender to replace the stud and stuff.||||reg||1
